      "IsMRef": true,
      "Title": "Virtufin.Api.Auth.ApiKeyAuthOptions",
      "Summary": "<p sourcefile=\"api/Virtufin.Api.Auth.ApiKeyAuthOptions.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"1\">API-key authentication configuration for the gRPC surface.\nKeys are named so successful calls can be attributed to a caller in logs.\nWhen no keys are configured, authentication is disabled (local dev default).</p>\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "ManagedReference",
      "source_relative_path": "api/Virtufin.Api.Auth.ApiKeyHttpMiddleware.yml",
      "output": {
        ".html": {
          "relative_path": "api/Virtufin.Api.Auth.ApiKeyHttpMiddleware.html"
        }
      },
      "version": "",
      "Uid": null,
      "IsMRef": true,
      "Title": "Virtufin.Api.Auth.ApiKeyHttpMiddleware",
      "Summary": "<p sourcefile=\"api/Virtufin.Api.Auth.ApiKeyHttpMiddleware.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"1\">Enforces <code>x-api-key</code> on the HTTP surface (the hand-written minimal-API\nendpoints such as <code>/v1/grpc/call</code>, the OpenAPI/Scalar docs, and\nJSON-transcoded gRPC). Native gRPC and gRPC-web calls carry their own\n<xref href=\"Virtufin.Api.Auth.ApiKeyInterceptor\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref> and are skipped here so they keep proper\ngRPC status codes. Health probes stay open.</p>\n<p sourcefile=\"api/Virtufin.Api.Auth.ApiKeyHttpMiddleware.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"7\">Without this, exposing the gRPC port through an ingress would also expose\nthose HTTP endpoints — which bypass the gRPC interceptor entirely — with no\nauthentication. Active only when <xref href=\"Virtufin.Api.Auth.ApiKeyAuthOptions.Enabled\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref>.</p>\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "ManagedReference",
      "source_relative_path": "api/Virtufin.Api.Auth.ApiKeyInterceptor.yml",
      "output": {
        ".html": {
          "relative_path": "api/Virtufin.Api.Auth.ApiKeyInterceptor.html"
        }
      },
      "version": "",
      "Uid": null,
      "IsMRef": true,
      "Title": "Virtufin.Api.Auth.ApiKeyInterceptor",
      "Summary": "<p sourcefile=\"api/Virtufin.Api.Auth.ApiKeyInterceptor.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"1\">Server interceptor enforcing <code>x-api-key</code> authentication on every gRPC\ncall (including JSON-transcoded ones) when <xref href=\"Virtufin.Api.Auth.ApiKeyAuthOptions.Enabled\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref>.\nHealth-check methods stay open so probes and load balancers keep working, and\nso do the Dapr sidecar's own app callbacks (see\n<xref href=\"Virtufin.Api.Auth.ApiKeyInterceptor.DaprAppCallbackPrefix\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref>).</p>\n"
    },
    {
